  "limitations": [
    "The 88-case feature sample retains 20 failures; these counts do not measure a global compatibility percentage.",
    "Inspection covers the admitted single-column immediate NO ACTION declarations. Composite/table-level declarations, other actions, deferred constraints and cross-table ALTER rename still need work.",
    "The exact unordered table iteration is tied to the pinned 64-bit default SQLite build. Alternative allocator/hash configurations, external concurrent schema changes and all schema-cache invalidation schedules have not been established by these examples.",
    "Parent matching uses supported scalar affinity and BINARY comparison. Other declared collations and WITHOUT ROWID metadata remain limited.",
    "The NULL-reference, insertion-length and unchanged-rollback proofs are component contracts, not proofs of whole-SQL/FK equivalence, complete cache refinement or physical crash behavior.",
    "Existing views/triggers, STRICT, UTF-16, generated columns, composite keys, expression/partial indexes and other SQL/storage gaps remain. The 60 SIGKILL samples cover existing storage paths rather than all FK inspection schedules."
  ],
